WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.123 --> 00:00:17.304
Jerry and his family were very sad about leaving their horses behind.

2
00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:19.284
I was sad too.

3
00:00:20.285 --> 00:00:23.685
I'd never known such a good master since my days at Birtwick Park.

4
00:00:25.486 --> 00:00:28.967
When the Governor heard what was happening, he offered to buy Hotspur.

5
00:00:30.727 --> 00:00:34.157
There were other cab drivers who would have taken me, but Jerry said no.

6
00:00:35.738 --> 00:00:37.860
He thought it was time to find me easier work.

7
00:00:39.461 --> 00:00:41.843
I was sold to a local baker who needed a horse.

8
00:00:43.545 --> 00:00:46.967
Jerry had known him for a long time and thought he'd give me a good home.

9
00:00:51.591 --> 00:00:52.672
In a way he was right.

10
00:00:53.493 --> 00:00:55.294
The baker himself was kind and fair.

11
00:00:57.376 --> 00:01:02.020
But he stayed busy in his shop, leaving the management of his delivery carts to his foreman.

12
00:01:03.532 --> 00:01:05.154
The foreman was always in a hurry.

13
00:01:05.714 --> 00:01:08.216
He often added more weight to an already full load.

14
00:01:10.138 --> 00:01:14.301
My driver, Jakes, sometimes protested when the foreman overloaded my cart.

15
00:01:14.321 --> 00:01:17.844
"This horse isn't young," Jakes would say.

16
00:01:17.864 --> 00:01:19.986
"He shouldn't pull so much weight."

17
00:01:20.006 --> 00:01:23.589
"Why make two trips if you can fit everything in one?"

18
00:01:23.909 --> 00:01:25.271
the foreman always replied.

19
00:01:25.291 --> 00:01:28.473
"Getting things done faster is better for business."

20
00:01:29.955 --> 00:01:31.376
The heavy loads were bad enough.

21
00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:38.042
To make things worse, all the drivers at this place used a checkrein, and Jakes was no exception.

22
00:01:39.103 --> 00:01:41.544
That made it difficult to pull even a normal load!

23
00:01:42.924 --> 00:01:47.726
By the time I'd been there a few months, I could already feel myself losing strength and spirit.

24
00:01:51.148 --> 00:01:54.109
One day my cart was loaded even more heavily than usual.

25
00:01:55.009 --> 00:01:57.410
Part of our route took us up a very steep hill.

26
00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:02.945
"Go on, Blackie," Jakes called, flicking the whip at me.

27
00:02:03.965 --> 00:02:07.947
I started up the hill, but could only go a short way before I had to stop.

28
00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:13.691
Jakes urged me on, and I took a few more steps before I had to rest again.

29
00:02:15.492 --> 00:02:16.932
Jakes began to lose patience.

30
00:02:16.952 --> 00:02:18.473
"Go on, you lazy fellow!"

31
00:02:18.793 --> 00:02:20.835
he called, whipping me a little harder.

32
00:02:22.736 --> 00:02:26.278
Once again I struggled on, pulling the heavy load a few more yards.

33
00:02:28.719 --> 00:02:31.901
When I stopped to catch my breath, I felt the whip cut me again.

34
00:02:33.622 --> 00:02:36.825
I surged forward, but I couldn't move the cart much farther.

35
00:02:37.805 --> 00:02:38.706
The whip came again.

36
00:02:40.187 --> 00:02:44.330
It pained me, but it hurt even more to know that I was being punished while doing my

37
00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:44.930
very best.

38
00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:47.772
"Excuse me, sir!"

39
00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:51.155
a sweet voice called out just as Jakes raised the whip again.

40
00:02:51.175 --> 00:02:54.177
"Please don't whip your horse anymore.

41
00:02:54.857 --> 00:02:58.060
The road is very steep, and I'm sure he's doing the best he can."

42
00:02:59.936 --> 00:03:01.577
The speaker was a fine-looking lady.

43
00:03:02.277 --> 00:03:04.658
Jakes gave her a respectful nod as he answered.

44
00:03:04.678 --> 00:03:10.300
"If doing his best won't get us where we're going, he'll have to do a little more," he

45
00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:14.822
said. "It looks like a very heavy load," the lady said.

46
00:03:14.842 --> 00:03:17.603
"Yes, it is," Jakes replied.

47
00:03:17.623 --> 00:03:19.564
"But that's not my fault.

48
00:03:20.665 --> 00:03:24.606
The foreman insisted on adding more to the cart, and now it's up to me to deliver it."

49
00:03:26.127 --> 00:03:27.147
He raised the whip again.

50
00:03:27.787 --> 00:03:28.968
The lady held up a hand.

51
00:03:30.104 --> 00:03:32.566
"Please, sir," she said in an earnest voice.

52
00:03:33.266 --> 00:03:35.188
"At least give the horse a fair chance.

53
00:03:36.448 --> 00:03:39.450
He can't use all his strength with his head held back that way.

54
00:03:40.731 --> 00:03:43.713
If you take off the checkrein, I'm sure he'll do better.

55
00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:47.096
Will you try it, please, as a favor to me?"

56
00:03:48.337 --> 00:03:50.778
Jakes looked surprised, but he tipped his hat.

57
00:03:50.798 --> 00:03:54.100
"Anything to please a lady," he said.

58
00:03:54.821 --> 00:03:56.482
"How far would you like me to loosen it, ma'am?"

59
00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:59.024
"All the way," she told him.

60
00:03:59.808 --> 00:04:00.869
"Just give him his head."

61
00:04:02.649 --> 00:04:04.150
Jakes shrugged and came forward.

62
00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:08.592
When he unbuckled the checkrein, I could hardly believe the relief!

63
00:04:11.273 --> 00:04:16.835
I stretched forward immediately, and tossed my head several times to shake the painful stiffness from my neck

64
00:04:16.875 --> 00:04:17.435
and shoulders.

65
00:04:17.455 --> 00:04:19.856
"Poor fellow!

66
00:04:19.916 --> 00:04:23.338
It looks like you needed that," the lady said, patting me.

67
00:04:24.558 --> 00:04:25.839
Jakes took me by the bridle.

68
00:04:25.859 --> 00:04:27.279
"Come on, Blackie.

69
00:04:27.539 --> 00:04:28.580
Let's give it another try."

70
00:04:29.916 --> 00:04:32.737
I put down my head and threw my strength against the load.

71
00:04:34.197 --> 00:04:37.898
The cart moved on, and this time I could pull it all the way up the hill.

72
00:04:39.439 --> 00:04:40.719
The lady walked along with us.

73
00:04:42.079 --> 00:04:44.620
When we reached the top, she gave me another pat.

74
00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:47.061
"There, you see?"

75
00:04:47.441 --> 00:04:49.121
she told Jakes with a sweet smile.

76
00:04:49.141 --> 00:04:54.083
"I hope you'll consider leaving off the checkrein from now on."

77
00:04:56.103 --> 00:04:58.484
When she left, Jakes shook his head.

78
00:04:59.596 --> 00:05:01.838
"That was a real lady," he said to himself.

79
00:05:01.858 --> 00:05:06.901
"She spoke to me as politely as if I were a gentleman rather than a humble cart driver."

80
00:05:09.362 --> 00:05:11.184
After that he loosened the checkrein a little.

81
00:05:11.924 --> 00:05:14.966
Even so, the heavy loads continued to wear me out.

82
00:05:16.927 --> 00:05:20.329
Before long the foreman brought in a younger horse to take my place.

83
00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:24.052
That left me to wonder once again what would become of me.
